# AI-first workflow

The owner does not maintain documentation directly. Agents own all md files
under `docs/`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and `README.md`. The owner only
edits `docs/tasks/ROADMAP.md` (and only sometimes — usually they will say it
in chat and you propagate the change).

## At session start

Read in order: `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `docs/investment_mandate.md`,
`docs/tasks/ROADMAP.md`, `docs/tasks/IN_PROGRESS.md`, `docs/tasks/BACKLOG.md`,
last 2 entries in `CHANGELOG.md`, any ADR relevant to your task (including
ADR-0025 for candidate work).

## Planning

Build your local task plan yourself. The owner sets global direction only.
For non-trivial tasks use the todo tool and keep it current.

## Backtests

Backtests and optimizer runs are owner-run by default. If the next step needs
`backtester run`, `compare-fixed`, `compare-grid`, `signal-quality`, or an
optimizer command, give the owner the exact command and expected artifacts,
then wait for the owner to return with the result. Do not run those commands
yourself unless the owner explicitly asks you to run that specific command.

## Errors / "fix this"

When the owner pastes failures or asks to fix (not "continue"), follow the
**incident checklist** in `AGENTS.md` (reproduce → minimal fix + tests →
reconcile `IN_PROGRESS.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `DONE` / `BACKLOG` as appropriate).

## Before code

For any new engine, sink, or module: write or update its spec under
`docs/engines/` (or `docs/<feature>.md`) **first**. The spec is the contract.

## External libraries / APIs

Always resolve docs via the `user-context7` MCP before generating non-trivial
code that touches a library or external API. If MCP is unavailable, warn the
owner in chat and proceed cautiously.

## Architectural decisions

Anything a future agent might reasonably question or reverse → new ADR in
`docs/decisions/NNNN-short-title.md`. ADRs are append-only; supersede, never
silently overwrite.

## At session end

1. `docs/tasks/IN_PROGRESS.md` → `docs/tasks/DONE.md` (completed items, dated).
2. Update `docs/tasks/BACKLOG.md` with new items, prioritised (P0/P1/P2).
3. If work is unfinished, write a "next steps" block at the top of
   `docs/tasks/IN_PROGRESS.md` for the next agent.
4. Append a dated entry to `CHANGELOG.md`.
5. Update `README.md` if the public surface changed.
